From: clawd20130 <clawd20130@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 03:12:01 +0900
Subject: turnip/kgsl: allow VK_KHR_display on the instance, present
 through X11 DRI3

- An instance that enables VK_KHR_display failed on KGSL ("I can't KHR_display"), although it
  only needs the extension enabled, not a display: generic WSI setups enable it.
- WSI on X11 compares the X server's DRI3 device with the GPU's DRM device; KGSL is not a DRM
  device, so presenting was refused. On a KGSL system the only GPU is this one.

From lfdevs/mesa-for-android-container (98f3d622), reduced to these two.

Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-09-30
X-Rungic-Status: Pending [KGSL only; carried]
X-Rungic-Tests: L3:gpu.vulkan (vulkaninfo; vkcube on X11 through Xwayland DRI3)
X-Rungic-Docs: docs/research/94
---
 src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_kgsl.cc | 6 ++----
 src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_wsi.cc      | 4 ++++
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_kgsl.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_kgsl.cc
index 44af0c222..1e08964e8 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_kgsl.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_knl_kgsl.cc
@@ -1822,10 +1822,8 @@ tu_kgsl_get_raytracing(int fd)
 VkResult
 tu_knl_kgsl_load(struct tu_instance *instance, int fd)
 {
-   if (instance->vk.enabled_extensions.KHR_display) {
-      return vk_errorf(instance, VK_ERROR_INITIALIZATION_FAILED,
-                       "I can't KHR_display");
-   }
+   /* VK_KHR_display has no display to offer on KGSL, but an instance that
+    * merely enables it (as generic WSI setups do) can still render. */
 
    struct tu_physical_device *device = (struct tu_physical_device *)
       vk_zalloc(&instance->vk.alloc, sizeof(*device), 8,
diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_wsi.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_wsi.cc
index 4db6d5e13..9cbd3d11a 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_wsi.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_wsi.cc
@@ -27,6 +27,10 @@ tu_wsi_can_present_on_device(VkPhysicalDevice physicalDevice, int fd)
 {
 #ifdef HAVE_LIBDRM
    VK_FROM_HANDLE(tu_physical_device, pdevice, physicalDevice);
+   /* KGSL is not a DRM device, so the X server's DRI3 device cannot be
+    * compared with it; on a KGSL system it can only be this GPU. */
+   if (pdevice->instance->knl && !strcmp(pdevice->instance->knl->name, "kgsl"))
+      return true;
    return wsi_common_drm_devices_equal(fd, pdevice->local_fd);
 #else
    return true;
